 2708 27D4 ~            ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 2709 27D4 ~            ; A product's or a quotient's operands, when both are normal numbers -- the common case, for
 2710 27D4 ~            ; which the general path's tests for NaNs, infinities, zeros and subnormals and its normalisation
 2711 27D4 ~            ; are all for nothing. Carry set if fpa or fpb is not one (an exponent field of 0 or 255), and
 2712 27D4 ~            ; then nothing is changed but fps, which the general path sets again. Otherwise, as that path
 2713 27D4 ~            ; would leave them: fps = the result's sign; the leading ones put into the significands, the low
 2714 27D4 ~            ; three bytes of fpa and fpb (__x80_fp_unpack); HL = a's exponent, BC = b's; D = b's top byte.
 2715 27D4 ~            ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
