 3519 27D4              ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 3520 27D4              ; Sixty-four bits: [HL] = [HL] op [DE], or [HL] shifted by the count in DE.
 3521 27D4              ;
 3522 27D4              ; The operands are eight bytes each, which no set of registers on this machine can hold, so these
 3523 27D4              ; take them by address -- the legaliser writes them into the caller's frame -- and work on copies
 3524 27D4              ; in static memory, a byte at a time. Simple and slow: the point for now is that long long works.
 3525 27D4              ; Multiplication is shift-and-add over sixty-four bits, division a restoring loop, sixty-four
